    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: unify `customerCode` + `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId`\n\nThe new `memberId` is formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` \u2014 region code, 2-digit fiscal year, the 8 upper-hex SHA-256-over-(normalizedTelephone+lastName) HASH8, and a Luhn check digit computed over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`. Example from the test run: `NSW2716E6609E1`.\n\n### New files\n- **`MemberId.java`** \u2014 assembles the base id (`<REGION><FY><HASH8>` + Luhn CHK) and holds the Luhn helper (moved from the deleted check-digit class).\n- **`AssignMemberId.java`** \u2014 the single pipeline step replacing the two old assign steps; derives region/FY/HASH8, builds the id, and applies collision de-duplication (`-<n>`) against existing `memberId`s.\n\n### Removed\n- `AssignCustomerCode.java`, `AssignMembershipNumber.java`, `CustomerCodeCheckDigit.java`\n- Owner fields `customerCode` + `membershipNumber` (and getters/setters), plus the `checkDigit` DTO mapping.\n- The `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, `checkDigit` schemas in `openapi.yml` (replaced with a `memberId` schema).\n\n### Updated\n- **Owner model** + all four DB schemas: `customer_code`/`membership_number` \u2192 single `member_id`; hsqldb seed `data.sql` positional inserts adjusted for the new column count.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`**: two steps collapsed into one `assignMemberId`.\n- **`OwnerIdentity`**: `primaryIdentifier` now returns `memberId`; `customerCodeHash` \u2192 `memberIdHash`.\n- **`CityRegion`**: `localityOfCustomerCode`/`timezoneOfCustomerCode` \u2192 `localityOfMemberId`/`timezoneOfMemberId`, parsing the region as the leading known region code (NSW/VIC/QLD/UNKNOWN) since the id has no dash separator.\n- **`OwnerSegment`** + **`OwnerMapper`**: reference `memberId` for locality/timezone/segment.\n- **`AuditOwnerCreated`**: audit line now carries `memberId` instead of `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`.\n\nOne deliberate non-change: `OwnerCreatedEvent`'s JSON key stays `customerCode` (it already carries `primaryIdentifier`, which now returns the `memberId` value) \u2014 its javadoc explicitly documented this as the stable serialization contract that follows the primary identifier without needing to change.\n\nFull suite: **Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0** \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
